{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125181-dark-eras-medieval-ireland-750-850-ce","id":1125181,"title":"[Dark Eras] Medieval Ireland 750-850 CE","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T04:53:44-07:00","id":1125181,"title":"[Dark Eras] Medieval Ireland 750-850 CE","content":"Whatever if Era wins or not race with Golden Age of S-F for <b>Dark Eras 2</b> corebook, I wanted to start discussion on it, even as fan based setting ideas. Lately we had some great topic in this vain about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion\">Arthurian Britain</a> or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1119302-britain-forsaken-by-rome\">Britain - Forsaken by Rome</a>. So maybe we asked nicely fan experts from those to look over this a bit fresher sister Era? Lord <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, Lord <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> ?<br /> <br /> Myself, I mostly look for <b>Werewolf</b> related material, using Medieval Ireland as sequel \u2013 or expansion \u2013 to <i>Wolf &amp; Raven </i>Viking Era from DE 1, in mostly the same time. But will gladly look over for other gamelines ideas if you bring them.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s start by quoting basic Era sum up from Kickstarter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following the Irish Dark Age until the beginning of the Viking Age, this era marks the introduction of Christianity and Latin literacy. The latter part of the period gives way to illuminated manuscripts, such as the Book of Kells, and Viking raiders who attack the coastline of Ailech and the rest of Ulster. In the Chronicles of Darkness, its denizens are used to the changes in leadership, but worry Viking raiders will discover their lairs and attack at will. This is an era of faith and fear, art and blade.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>So from it, important locations looks as Ailech and Ulster as general</b> \u2013 <b>What about them in this times you can say to us?</b> What are it\u2019s ethnics composition? How old are they Christian?<br /> <br /> I was thinking Era was centered on Dublin, but I then read in <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> this settlement was FOUNDED in 853, so 3 years after end of Era range. <b>What do you know about Dublin\u2019s origins?</b> You think it\u2019s just some omission on Era idea author?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-05-2017, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T06:03:34-07:00","id":1125188,"title":"","content":"well, if we were to get this Era, I hope for it to be at least partly Vampire, we would would finally get some more information about the Blood Blessed which were mentioned in Requiem for the Regina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T01:44:16-07:00","id":1125517,"title":"","content":"Medieval Ireland Era did not got to the book, but we still can make research and fan story hooks ourselves. Here are some questions some Irish forumers or historicians of period could answer me:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>When did Ireland been fully Christianized?</b> Are most Irelanders still 'pagan' in day to day life? Era idea sounds as Christianization was only a generation or two before, but I know that Irish bishops was sent 2 centuries before even to Iona Isle, for example.<br /> 2. <b>What does Ailech means in Era idea context?</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kings_of_Ailech\" target=\"_blank\">From Wikipedia</a>, I see it's Celtic ruling dynasty of land that will become Ireland.<br /> 3. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster\" target=\"_blank\">From Wikipedia</a>, again, it seems that Ulster was one of then bean kingdoms (later provinces) that would become Ireland. Most on the North one on Island, so most open to Norseman Vikings. Question then is this - <b>From what date Viking raids could start on Ulster?</b> First raid on Lindisfarne was in 793, so I suppose that few years later on Ulster could start?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T06:59:27-07:00","id":1303067,"title":"","content":"Book of Kells - Ireland's greatest early medieval artifact - is <a href=\"http://www.openculture.com/2019/03/the-medieval-masterpiece-the-book-of-kells-is-now-digitized-put-online.html\" target=\"_blank\">digitalised and ready to be seen by you all</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T17:41:20-07:00","id":1303852,"title":"","content":"An tricky ers for vampires, surely, as anything that could be construed as a city is only just beginning. Prior to the Vikings, there were no real cities in any serious sense in what becomes Ireland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avata